        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Guard AWS raw instance release by ownership tags",
        "body": "Closes https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/703.\n\n## Summary\n\n- reject direct AWS raw `i-*` resolution unless the instance carries the canonical `crabbox=true`, `created_by=crabbox`, `provider=aws`, canonical lease ID, and non-empty slug ownership tags\n- validate the resolved lease ID against the ownership tag before release and recheck canonical ownership at the provider delete boundary\n- skip and report noncanonical inventory entries during cleanup so one unowned instance cannot block cleanup of later valid leases\n- deliberately fail closed for unmanaged raw EC2 IDs in every resolution mode because ordinary connect/status flows can mutate lifecycle tags\n- add regression coverage and an Unreleased changelog entry thanking @TurboTheTurtle\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent exact head: `959e2866ba711c29a72dd5d57c21af6c0f84abd4`.\n\n- `go test -race ./internal/providers/aws`\n- `go test -race ./internal/providers/aws ./internal/cli`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `git diff --check`\n- autoreview accepted two findings, fixed both, then completed clean with no actionable findings; patch correct at 0.82 confidence\n- exact-head AWS direct-provider canary using a scratch broker-free config and a disposable on-demand lease:\n  - built the exact-head binary and passed provider doctor from a zero-resource baseline\n  - removed the canary's `created_by` ownership tag\n  - exact-head raw-instance stop failed closed with the expected unmanaged/canonical-ownership rejection\n  - independent EC2 state check confirmed the instance remained `running`\n  - restored the tag, stopped normally, and waited for EC2 termination\n  - provider key was absent and final Crabbox AWS inventory returned to the zero-resource baseline\n\nThe live credential came from 1Password and was kept only in the persistent validation session; no credential value or EC2 user data was printed or persisted in the repository.\n",
        "branch": "fix-crabbox-aws-stop-716",
